  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 6 and takes 25 minutes to prepare and 75 minutes to cook. Rfissa is a deeply sustaining dish of slow-braised chicken over a bed of torn flatbread or couscous soaked in a rich spiced broth, traditionally made with fenugreek."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: Traditional rfissa calls for "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "fenugreek-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "fenugreek"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " seeds, which give the broth its characteristic slightly bitter, mapley warmth. If you can source fenugreek seeds from a specialist grocer, add 1 teaspoon with the other spices. This version uses ras el hanout as the spice base, which carries a similar warming depth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
